From a265779ae69281209b36d10ced77463dfece1ab9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:52:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Pass input_origin to pre_llm_call
 (agent/human/unknown per client submit)

The coach complaint lane filed defects from agent-driven Desktop proof chats:
no signal told a pre_llm_call plugin whether a person or an agent script
(/api/ws?client=agent) wrote the turn.

- tui_gateway/human_input.input_origin(rid, params, text, *, transport, session)
  classifies a client prompt.submit: 'agent' (agent transport, agent_created or
  pending_hidden session, _turn_author/_hosted_* params, hidden widget intent,
  cross-session header), 'human' (is_human_typed_submit), else ''. note_submit
  reuses it and returns it; it still stamps only human submits.
- prompt.submit stashes the origin on the claimed session; _run_after_agent_ready
  consumes it and passes it to _run_prompt_submit, which sets agent._input_origin
  on EVERY turn (injected turns: Kanban notices, auto-continue, queued drains,
  prompt.admit -> ''). Faked helper signatures (_dispatch_admitted_prompt,
  _run_after_agent_ready) are unchanged.
- agent/turn_context passes input_origin=getattr(agent, '_input_origin', '') or ''
  to pre_llm_call (signature-filtered dispatch: narrow callbacks unaffected).
  CLI/gateway platforms leave it ''.

Proof: RED on origin/main (23 failed: no input_origin attr / hook kwarg KeyError /
turns ran with origin unset); GREEN 99 tests; 109 files importing the touched
seams 3436 passed; 15/15 mutants killed; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
